WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.140
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Tuesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.640
Who's in charge at Nvidia?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.100
Trump says he wouldn't mind if Jensen Huang came back.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.080
Over 165,000 people signed a letter to bring him back, Elon Musk included.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.350
Now, who's in charge of AI progress?

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.400
Anthropic says AI is already speeding up its own research.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.600
Its IPO filing says it's now met its own threshold for that,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.510
based on what it expects next.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.580
Its founders say the pace may need reining in, especially when AI builds AI.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.060
Last week, its Mythos model moved Claude onto AMD chips in three days.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.490
Normally? Months.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.870
In Washington,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.080
a new rule aims to shut a loophole that let Chinese firms rent top US chips abroad.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.730
And the White House reportedly plans to name over two dozen AI 'national champions',

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:13.790
Nvidia included.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.910
The Fed's chair, Kevin Warsh,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:22.360
called it superintelligence: "an entirely new force in economic life and society."

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.400
But he warned it could also disappoint: stocks fall,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.230
the economy slows, and unemployment rises.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.090
Some good news for science.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:37.030
OpenAI's giving free ChatGPT to up to 150,000 more researchers.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.190
And Apple's recruiting up to 200,000 people to study how we use AI for health.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.690
The catch?

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:50.610
Google saw hackers' AI agents hack websites with no human in the loop.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.600
OpenAI's letting outside testers check whether its AI tries to dodge control.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.290
Back to the machines.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:08.060
A robot called Iris is now partly steered by living human brain cells.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:14.220
In Malawi, a 25-year-old built an AI tool that's helping blind students excel.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:22.220
And a hacked PlayStation 4, from 2013, now runs an AI model. Fully offline.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.400
So, who's in charge? Still us. Let's make sure it stays that way.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
